Feature: UserRegistration
  @owner: "identity"
  @source: "usermgmt/es_decide.go"

Description:
  Registers users on the User aggregate (stream type User).
  A fresh stream with RegisterUser emits exactly one UserRegistered
  event; a duplicate registration is rejected with a conflict
  (usermgmt.user_already_exists).

Relationships:
  ProvidesTo: UserProfile, Membership, BotLifecycle

Scenario: Registering a new user
  @smoke, @user
  When a user registers
  Then events "UserRegistered" are emitted

Feature: UserProfile
  @owner: "identity"
  @source: "usermgmt/es_decide_profile.go"

Description:
  Email, display name, verification, credentials, and TOTP on the
  User aggregate. Changing the email un-verifies the account in the
  read model; verifying the email flips it back.

Relationships:
  DependsOn: UserRegistration

Scenario: Verifying the email flips the read model
  @user, @read-model
  Given a registered user
  When the email is verified
  Then events "EmailVerified" are emitted
    And the read model shows the email verified

Scenario: Changing the email un-verifies the account
  @user, @read-model
  Given a registered user with a verified email
  When the email is changed to "new@test.com"
  Then events "EmailChanged" are emitted
    And the read model shows the email unverified

Scenario: Display names change in sequence
  @user, @data-table
  Given a registered user
  When the display name changes to
    | name  |
    | Ada   |
    | Grace |
  Then events "DisplayNameChanged", "DisplayNameChanged" are emitted

Feature: TenantLifecycle
  @owner: "identity"
  @source: "usermgmt/es_tenant_decide.go"

Description:
  Tenant aggregate lifecycle: create, suspend, reactivate, delete.
  The suspended flag is a read-model projection of TenantSuspended
  and TenantReactivated.

Relationships:
  ProvidesTo: Membership

Scenario: Creating a tenant
  @smoke, @tenant, @read-model
  When a tenant named "acme" is created
  Then events "TenantCreated" are emitted
    And the read model shows the tenant name "acme"

Scenario: Suspending a created tenant
  @tenant, @read-model
  Given a tenant named "acme"
  When the tenant is suspended for "policy violation"
  Then events "TenantSuspended" are emitted
    And the read model shows the tenant suspended

Scenario: Reactivating a suspended tenant
  @tenant, @read-model
  Given a suspended tenant named "acme"
  When the tenant is reactivated
  Then events "TenantReactivated" are emitted
    And the read model shows the tenant not suspended

Scenario: Deleting a tenant
  @tenant
  Given a tenant named "acme"
  When the tenant is deleted for "shutdown"
  Then events "TenantDeleted" are emitted

Feature: Membership
  @owner: "identity"
  @source: "usermgmt/es_membership_decide.go"

Description:
  Membership aggregates keyed by DeriveMembershipID(actor, tenant):
  add, change roles, remove. The decider is local — adding a member
  to an empty stream emits MemberAdded without tenant pre-existence.

Relationships:
  DependsOn: UserRegistration, TenantLifecycle

Scenario: Adding a member to a tenant
  @smoke, @membership
  When a member with roles "admin" is added
  Then events "MemberAdded" are emitted

Scenario: Updating member roles
  @membership
  Given a member with roles "admin"
  When the member roles change to "admin, writer"
  Then events "MemberRolesChanged" are emitted

Scenario: Removing a member
  @membership
  Given a member with roles "admin"
  When the member is removed
  Then events "MemberRemoved" are emitted

Feature: BotLifecycle
  @owner: "identity"
  @source: "usermgmt/es_bot_decide.go"

Description:
  Bot aggregate lifecycle: register with owner, token hash and
  scopes; delete with a reason.

Relationships:
  DependsOn: UserRegistration

Scenario: Registering a bot
  @smoke, @bot
  When a bot named "deploy-bot" is registered
  Then events "BotRegistered" are emitted

Scenario: Retiring a bot
  @bot
  Given a registered bot named "deploy-bot"
  When the bot is deleted for "retired"
  Then events "BotDeleted" are emitted

Feature: AuthAudit
  @owner: "identity"
  @source: "usermgmt/auth_audit.go"

Description:
  Auth audit journal (LoginSucceeded, LoginFailed,
  RegistrationClosed, SessionStarted, SessionEnded) on dedicated
  Auth-typed streams. Emitted by the service layer around login and
  session flows — not by a decider, so no executable scenarios here.

Relationships:
  EmitsTo: AuditJournal with events="LoginSucceeded, LoginFailed, RegistrationClosed, SessionStarted, SessionEnded"

Feature: AuditJournal
  @owner: "identity"
  @source: "usermgmt/audit_log.go"

Description:
  The AuditLog subscribes to the full user lifecycle plus the auth
  audit journal (allAuditedEventTypes). Tenant, membership and bot
  events are NOT audited.

Relationships:
  ListensFrom: UserRegistration with events="UserRegistered, UserDeleted"
  ListensFrom: UserProfile with events="EmailChanged, DisplayNameChanged, EmailVerified, TOTPEnabled, TOTPDisabled, CredentialAdded, CredentialRemoved, CredentialUsed, ExternalAccountLinked, ExternalAccountUnlinked"
  ListensFrom: AuthAudit with events="LoginSucceeded, LoginFailed, RegistrationClosed, SessionStarted, SessionEnded"
